[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Tutorial: Stored Procedures and Database Functions in JPA"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Java Persistence API (JPA) provides robust support for calling database stored procedures and native functions. This allows developers to leverage database-specific performance optimizations, complex business logic encapsulated in the database, and custom SQL functions directly from their Java application."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Defining a Stored Procedure Query"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"To call a stored procedure in JPA, you typically use the EntityManager.createStoredProcedureQuery() method. You must specify the name of the stored procedure as defined in your database."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"StoredProcedureQuery query = entityManager.createStoredProcedureQuery('get_employee_by_dept');
query.registerStoredProcedureParameter('dept_id', Long.class, ParameterMode.IN);
query.setParameter('dept_id', 10L);

List<Object[]> results = query.getResultList();"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Mapping Stored Procedure Results to Entities"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"If your stored procedure returns a result set that matches an existing entity, you can pass the entity class as the second parameter to createStoredProcedureQuery to automatically map the results."},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"StoredProcedureQuery query = entityManager.createStoredProcedureQuery('get_active_users', User.class);
query.registerStoredProcedureParameter('status_param', String.class, ParameterMode.IN);
query.setParameter('status_param', 'ACTIVE');

List<User> users = query.getResultList();"},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Using IN, OUT, and INOUT Parameters"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"Stored procedures frequently use OUT and INOUT parameters to return single values or status codes. You can register these parameters using ParameterMode and retrieve their values after executing the query."},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"StoredProcedureQuery query = entityManager.createStoredProcedureQuery('calculate_bonus');
query.registerStoredProcedureParameter('emp_id', Long.class, ParameterMode.IN);
query.registerStoredProcedureParameter('bonus_amount', Double.class, ParameterMode.OUT);

query.setParameter('emp_id', 105L);
query.execute();

Double bonus = (Double) query.getOutputParameterValue('bonus_amount');"},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"4. Utilizing Named Stored Procedures via Annotations"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"You can declare stored procedures at the entity level using the @NamedStoredProcedureQuery annotation. This centralizes your queries and makes them reusable across your codebase."},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"@Entity
@NamedStoredProcedureQuery(
    name = 'User.updateStatus',
    procedureName = 'update_user_status',
    parameters = {
        @StoredProcedureParameter(name = 'userId', type = Long.class, mode = ParameterMode.IN),
        @StoredProcedureParameter(name = 'newStatus', type = String.class, mode = ParameterMode.IN)
    }
)
public class User {
    // Entity fields, getters, setters
}"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"Once named, you can invoke the procedure using the name you assigned in the annotation."},{"order":16,"type":"code","text":"StoredProcedureQuery query = entityManager.createNamedStoredProcedureQuery('User.updateStatus');
query.setParameter('userId', 42L);
query.setParameter('newStatus', 'SUSPENDED');
query.execute();"},{"order":17,"type":"subheading","text":"5. Calling Database Functions in JPQL"},{"order":18,"type":"paragraph","text":"Database functions can be called directly inside JPQL or Criteria API queries using the function() keyword. This is especially useful for string manipulation, mathematical operations, or date functions."},{"order":19,"type":"code","text":"String jpql = 'SELECT u FROM User u WHERE FUNCTION("YEAR", u.createdDate) = :year';
List<User> users = entityManager.createQuery(jpql, User.class)
    .setParameter('year', 2023)
    .getResultList();"},{"order":20,"type":"bullet_point","text":"ParameterMode.IN is used for input parameters passed to the procedure."},{"order":21,"type":"bullet_point","text":"ParameterMode.OUT and ParameterMode.INOUT are used to retrieve values computed inside the procedure."},{"order":22,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always ensure transaction boundaries are properly handled when executing modifying stored procedures."}]
